## Hints for Future Agents
The syntax is wta <branch-name> [base-branch]. Existing behavior already used the current HEAD, not a hardcoded main or master branch. An explicit base is rejected when the target branch already exists, so it cannot silently ignore the requested base or reset an existing branch. The aliases file is sourced by both Bash and Zsh. Existing interactive shells need to source the aliases file again. The post-commit hook automatically pushes master and may rebase; bypass it when a note must be attached before pushing. Push master and refs/notes/commits together after attaching this note.

## Codebase Discoveries
There is no dedicated test suite for these shell aliases. Temporary shared local clones provide real worktree coverage without creating test commits. Worktrees use the current directory basename under ~/.herdr/worktrees, and branch slashes become dashes in directory names. Selecting a base only sets the starting commit; this function does not create a PR or configure its target branch.

